WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.247 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
A number is hidden, but the relationship is still there.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:07.912 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Today we are finding missing values using addition and
subtraction.

00:00:08.132 --> 00:00:15.149 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
We will think about parts and totals, reverse an operation,
and put our answer back into the original sentence to check
it.

00:00:15.799 --> 00:00:21.433 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Our learning goal is to find missing values using parts,
totals and inverse operations.

00:00:22.083 --> 00:00:23.840 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Success criteria.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.275 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
I can identify which part or total is missing.

00:00:27.495 --> 00:00:30.438 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
I can choose the matching inverse operation.

00:00:30.658 --> 00:00:33.860 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
I can put the answer back to check the number sentence.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.910 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Addition joins parts into a total.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.657 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Subtraction can find a missing part.

00:00:39.877 --> 00:00:45.801 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Read the whole number sentence before choosing an operation:
the position of the missing value matters.

00:00:46.451 --> 00:00:50.874 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
A missing number plus two hundred and seventy-five equals
nine hundred.

00:00:51.094 --> 00:00:54.796 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Nine hundred is the total, so subtract the known part.

00:00:55.446 --> 00:00:58.550 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
The missing part is six hundred and twenty-five.

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:06.291 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Substitute it into the original sentence: six hundred and
twenty-five plus two hundred and seventy-five equals nine
hundred.

00:01:06.941 --> 00:01:11.739 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Now eight hundred minus a missing number equals three
hundred and forty-five.

00:01:11.959 --> 00:01:15.789 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
The starting total is eight hundred; the removed part is
unknown.

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:19.567 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
The removed part is four hundred and fifty-five.

00:01:19.962 --> 00:01:22.542 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Check by subtracting it from eight hundred.

00:01:22.762 --> 00:01:26.352 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
We return to three hundred and forty-five, as required.

00:01:27.002 --> 00:01:31.076 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
It is tempting to subtract just because you see a
subtraction sign.

00:01:31.296 --> 00:01:35.237 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
But a missing starting total needs the removed part added
back.

00:01:35.457 --> 00:01:41.367 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
For a blank minus two hundred and fifty equals five hundred,
add those two known parts, then check.

00:01:42.017 --> 00:01:46.652 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
A missing number minus one hundred and eighty equals four
hundred and twenty.

00:01:46.872 --> 00:01:48.770 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
What was the starting number?

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:58.545 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Add the removed part back: four hundred and twenty plus one
hundred and eighty is six hundred.

00:01:58.765 --> 00:02:03.342 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Check: six hundred minus one hundred and eighty is four
hundred and twenty.

00:02:03.992 --> 00:02:06.557 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Identify the total and the parts.

00:02:06.777 --> 00:02:13.018 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Use inverse operations to find the unknown, then substitute
your answer into the original sentence.

00:02:13.238 --> 00:02:16.901 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
A check tests the relationship, not just the arithmetic.

00:02:17.121 --> 00:02:20.278 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Now choose a strategy and explain why it works.
